<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Radegast</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Radegast is a name linked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rethra">Rethra</a>, the chief sanctuary of the West Slavic Lutici. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thietmar-of-merseburg">Thietmar of Merseburg</a>, writing around 1015, called the place Riedegost and its main god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svarozic">Zuarasici</a> (Svarožič), while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-of-bremen">Adam of Bremen</a> in the 1070s named the god himself Radegast. Later tradition made Radegast a Slavic god of hospitality and war.</p></div>
